editorialMd:
The working idea

Insert all readings into a binary min-heap and repeatedly remove the smallest. Produce that removal sequence, preserving duplicates.

Return the first value in the derived sequence that is at least k, or -1 if there is none. Return the value, not its index.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n log n); space O(n).

javascript
function priorityBasketFirstQualifyingSlip(readings, k) {
  const a=readings; let out=[];
  const heap=[];for(const x of a){heap.push(x);let i=heap.length-1;while(i){const p=(i-1)>>1;if(heap[p]<=heap[i])break;[heap[p],heap[i]]=[heap[i],heap[p]];i=p;}}while(heap.length){out.push(heap[0]);const last=heap.pop();if(!heap.length)break;heap[0]=last;let i=0;while(true){let j=i,l=2*i+1,r=l+1;if(l<heap.length&&heap[l]<heap[j])j=l;if(r<heap.length&&heap[r]<heap[j])j=r;if(j===i)break;[heap[i],heap[j]]=[heap[j],heap[i]];i=j;}}
  return out.find(x=>x>=k)??-1;
}


